# Copy to .env.local if you need it. .env.local is git-ignored.
#
# You almost certainly do not. The image host is a committed constant in
# vite.config.ts, because it is a public URL that appears in every <img src>
# the site serves — not a secret, so not a variable.
#
# This overrides it, for pointing a local build at somewhere else. Absolute
# URL, no trailing slash. Leave it empty and dev falls back to /res/img, the
# symlink under apps/elmapt/public/res, so a fresh checkout runs with no setup
# at all.
#
#   VITE_RES_BASE=https://staging.example.com
#
# Do NOT set this in Netlify. A declared environment variable whose value
# turns up in the build output is exactly what the secret scanner fails on.

VITE_RES_BASE=
